spa-reference Repository Version History
====================================================

v1.0 (2026-10-04)
-----------------
- Initial release.

Version History Guidelines
==========================
- Record externally meaningful or architecturally significant outcomes, not a
  diary of implementation work.
- Omit development-time corrections and intermediate states that were reverted
  or superseded before release. Git history retains that detail.
- Summarize related low-level changes under their substantive outcome.
- Write one coherent change per bullet, at most two physical lines.
- A single line at or under 80 columns is preferred whenever practical.
  Names and identifiers necessary to describe the change may pass 80 columns
  on the bullet's one or two lines when they cannot be shortened without
  losing meaning.
- When a version history already exists, balance a new entry against the
  length of the existing lines, so that the whole file stays consistent.
  Holding to the form this file has settled on comes before the two-line,
  80-column limit above, and leaves that limit standing wherever no such
  form exists.
- When an entry becomes substantially longer, omit or abstract implementation
  details, examples, reasons, and secondary effects where possible.
- Preserve the changed target, externally observable behavior, compatibility,
  privacy and security impact, and important names and identifiers.
- Combine related changes within the same version, especially changes to the
  same file or feature.
- Place closely related entries near each other.
- Append an independent new change to the end of the current version entry.
- Never create more than one repository version for the same calendar date.
- Independent changes may use separate bullets, but they stay in that day's
  single version entry.
- Past entries and their dates are a record. Do not rewrite, renumber or merge
  them. Past releases that share a date stay recorded as they were made. They
  do not conform to the rule above and are not precedent for new releases.
- The first entry, at the lowest version this file reaches, reads only
  "Initial release." and nothing else.
- An unreleased entry carries (Release Date: TBD). Replacing TBD with the
  actual date is the release itself, and is not a change to record here.
- This file records the history of the repository. A change that is not
  observable from outside does not need an entry here, and a documentation
  only change takes none unless its scale makes it worth one line saying so.
- Where individual source files carry their own Version History, that history
  records changes to the file independently of the repository release history.
  A repository release entry does not raise a source-file version, and a
  source-file version change does not by itself require a repository release
  entry. Record it here only when the change meets the repository-level
  criteria above.
- Recording a repository version here does not create or require a Git tag or
  GitHub Release. Either is created only when the maintainer explicitly asks
  for it.
